From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Birk Skyum <birk.skyum@pm.me>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 22:31:18 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] soc: qcom: aoss: Add a parameter that keeps the AOSS out
 of sleep

Some boards don't come back from AOSS sleep. On the Samsung Galaxy
Book4 Edge 14 a deep suspend with it allowed loses UFS on resume, and
an s2idle one ends in a PMIC power cycle once a full hour of the AOP
clock passes. With AOSS sleep disabled both sleep normally.

The prevent_aoss_sleep debugfs entry can disable it, but only after
boot, and not under lockdown. Add a prevent_aoss_sleep module
parameter that sends the same message at probe, so a board's kernel
command line can keep the AOSS out of sleep from the first suspend.

Link: https://github.com/omacom/omarchy/discussions/15860#discussioncomment-19637292
Signed-off-by: Birk Skyum <birk.skyum@pm.me>
---
 drivers/soc/qcom/qcom_aoss.c | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/soc/qcom/qcom_aoss.c b/drivers/soc/qcom/qcom_aoss.c
index a4ec434..4508f67 100644
--- a/drivers/soc/qcom/qcom_aoss.c
+++ b/drivers/soc/qcom/qcom_aoss.c
@@ -488,6 +488,10 @@ void qmp_put(struct qmp *qmp)
 }
 EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(qmp_put);
 
+static bool prevent_aoss_sleep;
+module_param(prevent_aoss_sleep, bool, 0444);
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(prevent_aoss_sleep, "Keep the AOSS out of sleep from probe on, for boards that fail to resume from it");
+
 struct qmp_debugfs_entry {
 	const char *name;
 	const char *fmt;
@@ -621,6 +625,12 @@ static int qmp_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 
 	platform_set_drvdata(pdev, qmp);
 
+	if (prevent_aoss_sleep) {
+		ret = qmp_send(qmp, "{class: aoss_slp, res: sleep, val: disable}");
+		if (ret)
+			dev_warn(&pdev->dev, "failed to keep the AOSS out of sleep: %d\n", ret);
+	}
+
 	qmp_debugfs_create(qmp);
 
 	return 0;
-- 
